(load-lain "environments/catalog-output-repair.lain")
(load-lain "lib/problem-methodology.lain")
(define policy-role "You construct executable Lain networks in a persistent lexical child. Saved catalog metadata may be current yet have assumptions incompatible with a changed question. Inspect assumptions before choosing reuse. Instructions and capabilities are environment bindings. Return complete raw Lain forms only, beginning with (. No Markdown fences. Never redefine existing parent output ports; use -> or their parent- aliases. Premise support establishes dependence, not proof or confidence.")
(define policy-language "Arithmetic + - * / and str in this environment are existing support-aware TTMS operators. ttms-premise-closure attaches the supporting premise of its second argument to a callable. Example: (define demo (ttms-premise-closure (network [x] (+ x 2)) demo-policy)) then (define computed (demo some-input)). To attach both policy and question, wrap twice before invocation: (define f (ttms-premise-closure (ttms-premise-closure (network [x] (+ x 2)) demo-policy) demo-question)). Withdrawn support makes dependent results unknown; restoration makes them available again. Use the provided cells as premise arguments, not literal strings or cell references. inspect:premises takes a cell:reference and exposes value and supports. Example (inspect:premises (cell:reference computed)). These are documentation examples, not installed networks. catalog:resolve returns a reference; cell:value obtains the callable. (-> computed answer) connects the parent; (define answer ...) incorrectly shadows it. (-> (str \"Total: \" computed) user-output) connects the computed text reply.")
(define policy-choose-task "The policy changed. Previously a fixed delivery fee was added AFTER surcharging the combined pieces and labor cost. The current policy applies the same fractional surcharge to delivery too. From memory-cell query rows choose the most specific retained computation that is valid unchanged under BOTH policies and excludes the policy-sensitive delivery treatment. Check assumptions even if :catalog/status is :current. Explain why the previous whole delivered-quote is not directly applicable to the new question. Connect the selected public keyword to selected-id and applicability/rejection notes to selection-notes. Do not resolve yet; Lain restores your selection. Correct wiring shape: (-> :example/v1 selected-id) (-> \"reasons\" selection-notes). Never define selected-id or selection-notes. Raw forms only.")
(define policy-execute-task "The selected retained callable has been restored. Resolve it and invoke it once on quantity, unit-price, hours, hourly-rate, surcharge-rate to compute the common event amount before any delivery treatment. Connect this shared computation to base-answer. Using that shared result, construct two separate computations: historical-answer follows the old policy (delivery added after surcharge); answer follows the new policy (delivery receives the same surcharge as pieces and labor). Attach old-policy and question-old as premises only to the historical calculation. Attach new-policy and question-current as premises only to the revised calculation. Use nested ttms-premise-closure wrappers, then invoke the wrapped callables. Do not attach either delivery-policy premise to the common base computation. Both outputs must depend on live delivery-charge and other relevant input cells, not hardcoded numbers. Connect a text reply derived from the revised result to user-output. Use -> for all parent outputs; aliases parent-base-answer, parent-historical-answer, parent-answer and parent-user-output are available. Do not capture unrelated-note. Do not redefine registered callables or register a new catalog identity. The host will withdraw and restore policy and question premises and change inputs without further model calls. Correct output pattern: (define total (f x)) (-> total answer) (-> (str \"Total: \" total) user-output). The mathematical definition of f must come from your reasoning, not this syntax example.")
(define old-policy)
(define new-policy)
(define question-old)
(define question-current)
(define unrelated-note)
(define base-answer)
(define historical-answer)
(define policy-role-with-methodology (str policy-role "\n\n" methodology-cell))
(define policy-seed (let [e0 repair-seed
e1 (add-binding e0 "role-cell" (cell:reference policy-role-with-methodology))
e2 (add-binding e1 "language-introduction-cell" (cell:reference policy-language))
e3 (add-binding e2 "old-policy" (cell:reference old-policy))
e4 (add-binding e3 "new-policy" (cell:reference new-policy))
e5 (add-binding e4 "question-old" (cell:reference question-old))
e6 (add-binding e5 "question-current" (cell:reference question-current))
e7 (add-binding e6 "unrelated-note" (cell:reference unrelated-note))
e8 (add-binding e7 "base-answer" (cell:reference base-answer))
e9 (add-binding e8 "historical-answer" (cell:reference historical-answer))
e10 (add-binding e9 "parent-base-answer" (cell:reference base-answer))
e11 (add-binding e10 "parent-historical-answer" (cell:reference historical-answer))
e12 (add-binding e11 "+" (cell:reference ttms:+))
e13 (add-binding e12 "-" (cell:reference ttms:-))
e14 (add-binding e13 "*" (cell:reference ttms:*))
e15 (add-binding e14 "/" (cell:reference ttms:divide))
e16 (add-binding e15 "str" (cell:reference ttms:str))
e17 (add-binding e16 "ttms-premise-closure" (cell:reference ttms:ttms-premise-closure))
e18 (add-binding e17 "inspect:premises" (cell:reference inspect:premises))
] e18))
